PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Key split in round 0: 5 colleagues pick A (mainly arguing GP corp in LP lacks clear AI status or LP balance-sheet proof), 4 pick E (net-asset test for entity fails because investment-property values unknown, only GIC + $300k liabilities shown; owners Alex/Bob also fail individual tests), 1 picks C (exactly $5M net assets allegedly insufficient), 1 picks D (James fails income test so entity (m) unavailable).  
Exact NI 45-106 tests recalled: individual income >$200k/$300k spousal; net financial assets >$1M; net assets >=$5M; entity net assets >=$5M on FS or all owners AIs. Wording is "at least $5M", so C qualifies.  
Strongest arguments: E cannot confirm >=$5M net assets (unknown property values) and owners not AIs; A succeeds because LPs meet individual tests + GP corp has $6M cash (qualifies under entity test) + all owners therefore AIs. D and B clearly pass. Unresolved: whether any colleague misreads "at least" vs "exceed". Current lean: E is the non-AI.}

